@startuml 030 Intent-Aware Chunking Lifecycle
' Document processing state (unchanged) and the backfill transition
' NOTE: no !theme directive for renderer compatibility
[*] --> Uploading : POST /api/documents (staged, original stored)
Uploading --> Queued : published to work queue
Queued --> Indexing : worker picks up
Indexing --> Ready : two-level index persisted
Indexing --> Failed : extraction/embed/upsert error
Failed --> Uploading : re-upload same bytes (retry, reason cleared)
Ready --> Uploading : startup backfill (no parent row yet)
Ready --> [*] : DELETE /api/documents
Failed --> [*] : DELETE /api/documents

note right of Indexing : Chunking now also persists\nparent rows (Level=Parent)
note right of Ready : Backfill re-indexes Ready docs\nlacking a parent row - idempotent (FR-011)
@enduml
